1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,695
Sunday night.

2
00:00:01,795 --> 00:00:03,332
Three deadlines.

3
00:00:03,432 --> 00:00:04,799
Zero plan.

4
00:00:05,299 --> 00:00:06,516
An essay.

5
00:00:06,616 --> 00:00:08,388
Two chapters to read.

6
00:00:08,488 --> 00:00:10,324
And a quiz on Friday.

7
00:00:10,824 --> 00:00:16,031
So you open your laptop, and somehow, an hour of scrolling later, nothing has started.

8
00:00:16,531 --> 00:00:18,623
The problem usually isn't you.

9
00:00:18,723 --> 00:00:21,071
The task is just too big to start.

10
00:00:22,371 --> 00:00:26,468
In the next three minutes, let's turn that mess into a plan for your week.

11
00:00:26,968 --> 00:00:28,228
Three moves.

12
00:00:28,328 --> 00:00:29,567
Smash it.

13
00:00:29,667 --> 00:00:30,842
Slot it.

14
00:00:30,942 --> 00:00:32,031
Check it.

15
00:00:32,531 --> 00:00:37,802
And stay until the end, because there's one slot most plans forget to leave empty.

16
00:00:39,102 --> 00:00:40,277
Move one.

17
00:00:40,377 --> 00:00:41,616
Smash it.

18
00:00:42,116 --> 00:00:43,845
Take the biggest task.

19
00:00:43,945 --> 00:00:45,397
Write the essay.

20
00:00:45,897 --> 00:00:48,117
You can't finish that in one sitting.

21
00:00:48,217 --> 00:00:49,541
So break it.

22
00:00:50,041 --> 00:00:51,472
Choose a topic.

23
00:00:51,972 --> 00:00:53,637
Find three sources.

24
00:00:54,137 --> 00:00:55,589
Write an outline.

25
00:00:56,089 --> 00:00:57,626
Draft the intro.

26
00:00:58,126 --> 00:00:59,578
Draft the body.

27
00:01:00,078 --> 00:01:01,594
Edit and submit.

28
00:01:02,094 --> 00:01:03,546
Six pieces.

29
00:01:03,646 --> 00:01:07,829
Each one starts with a verb, and each one has a clear finish line.

30
00:01:08,329 --> 00:01:09,610
Quick test.

31
00:01:09,710 --> 00:01:12,186
Could you start it in the next five minutes?

32
00:01:12,286 --> 00:01:14,207
If not, smash it again.

33
00:01:14,707 --> 00:01:16,628
Now the reading and the quiz.

34
00:01:16,728 --> 00:01:18,223
Four more pieces.

35
00:01:18,723 --> 00:01:21,903
Three scary tasks just became ten small ones.

36
00:01:23,203 --> 00:01:24,399
Move two.

37
00:01:24,499 --> 00:01:25,674
Slot it.

38
00:01:26,174 --> 00:01:27,583
Here's your week.

39
00:01:27,683 --> 00:01:29,306
But don't fill it yet.

40
00:01:29,806 --> 00:01:32,325
First, block out what's already taken.

41
00:01:32,425 --> 00:01:33,664
Classes.

42
00:01:33,764 --> 00:01:34,811
Work.

43
00:01:34,911 --> 00:01:36,043
Meals.

44
00:01:36,143 --> 00:01:37,254
Rest.

45
00:01:37,754 --> 00:01:40,230
What's left is your real study time.

46
00:01:40,330 --> 00:01:44,534
In this example, about an hour on weeknights, and more on Saturday.

47
00:01:45,034 --> 00:01:47,638
Your week will look different, and that's fine.

48
00:01:48,138 --> 00:01:49,889
Deadlines go first.

49
00:01:49,989 --> 00:01:53,169
The quiz is on Friday, so the reading lands early.

50
00:01:53,669 --> 00:01:55,804
The essay pieces fill the gaps.

51
00:01:56,304 --> 00:01:58,609
And remember that slot I mentioned?

52
00:01:58,709 --> 00:01:59,948
Here it is.

53
00:02:00,448 --> 00:02:02,348
Leave one slot empty.

54
00:02:02,448 --> 00:02:03,751
On purpose.

55
00:02:04,251 --> 00:02:07,431
Because something usually takes longer than you expect.

56
00:02:08,731 --> 00:02:09,970
Move three.

57
00:02:10,070 --> 00:02:11,159
Check it.

58
00:02:11,659 --> 00:02:14,754
Every night, take two minutes and tick off what's done.

59
00:02:15,254 --> 00:02:16,365
Monday.

60
00:02:16,465 --> 00:02:17,448
Done.

61
00:02:17,548 --> 00:02:18,765
Tuesday.

62
00:02:18,865 --> 00:02:19,848
Done.

63
00:02:20,348 --> 00:02:21,501
Wednesday.

64
00:02:21,601 --> 00:02:23,373
The outline ran long.

65
00:02:23,873 --> 00:02:25,133
No panic.

66
00:02:25,233 --> 00:02:27,368
That's what the empty slot is for.

67
00:02:27,868 --> 00:02:29,469
Move it to Saturday.

68
00:02:29,569 --> 00:02:31,938
The plan bends instead of breaking.

69
00:02:32,438 --> 00:02:35,383
And if a piece keeps slipping, it's still too big.

70
00:02:35,483 --> 00:02:36,892
Smash it again.

71
00:02:37,392 --> 00:02:40,081
At the end of the week, ask two questions.

72
00:02:40,581 --> 00:02:41,820
What worked?

73
00:02:41,920 --> 00:02:44,076
And what will I change next week?

74
00:02:45,376 --> 00:02:47,127
So that's the whole method.

75
00:02:47,227 --> 00:02:48,466
Smash it.

76
00:02:48,566 --> 00:02:49,741
Slot it.

77
00:02:49,841 --> 00:02:50,930
Check it.

78
00:02:51,430 --> 00:02:53,309
You don't need a perfect plan.

79
00:02:53,409 --> 00:02:55,586
You need one you'll actually start.

80
00:02:56,086 --> 00:02:59,373
Pick one task tonight, and smash it into pieces.

81
00:02:59,873 --> 00:03:01,574
Thanks for watching.
